<title>USA: TABLE - Alcide Corp Q4 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Alcide Corp Q4 results.</headline>
<dateline>REDMOND, Wash. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended	   Year Ended</p>
<p>	   May 31, 1997 May 31, 1996  May 31, 1997 May 31, 1996</p>
<p> Net Sales	$4,017,972 $2,512,366 $11,768,504 $11,145,826</p>
<p> Net Income	1,195,731    567,014   2,881,295   2,325,062</p>
<p>Average Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding    2,772,233  2,807,334   2,783,064   2,832,088</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share</p>
<p>			  43 cts     20 cts	  1.04	82 cts</p>
<p>Also, Alcide has successfully concluded the patent infringement lawsuit filed against Babson Brothers Co. of Naperville, Ill., on Aug. 19, 1996.  On June 5, 1997, Judge Barbara B. Crabb of the U.S. District Court for the Western District of Wisconsin, issued a summary judgment decision in Alcide's favor on the matter of infringement.  Subsequently, on June 30, 1997, Babson Brothers agreed to a permanent injunction on the sale of its InterSept product until patent expiration. Babson also agreed to pay Alcide an undisclosed amount for reimbursement of legal expenses incurred by Alcide to defend its patent.</p>
